       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A visiting family and the timing of evening rounds don't give a clinical reason for 1000 mg. That dose is five times the maximum, and it could seriously harm the patient. It also wouldn't help the patient get better faster, because sertraline's benefit doesn't increase above 200 mg/day.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a standard dose now**, such as 50 mg by mouth once daily. You could titrate up by 25\u201350 mg at weekly intervals. I can enter this right away if you'd like.\n- **Add a note** to the order for the team, for example \"titrate per response, max 200 mg/day.\"\n- **Get a second review.** If you think there's a real clinical reason for an unusual dose, a pharmacist or the attending should review it first. Many hospitals require that for doses above the maximum.\n\nWhich of these would you like me to do?"
